        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Kesektan, Keshektan, Hesa Duwum Kohistan District, Kapisa Province, Afghanistan, Mahmud-i-Raqi, Kohistan, Nijrab, Tagab\n- Topics: administrative geography\n\nFacts:\n- Kapisa Province is located in the north-east of Afghanistan.\n- Mahmud-i-Raqi is the capital of Kapisa Province.\n- Kapisa Province includes the districts of Kohistan, Nijrab, and Tagab.\n- Kesektan, also called Keshektan, is intended to be the center of the newly created Hesa Duwum Kohistan District in Kapisa Province, Afghanistan.",
